  "id": "COMPOUND:30209 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "Licoagroside D is implicated in the regulation of Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5, through a multi-step pathway involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This complex is targeted by multiple compounds, including (+)-Phylliroside, quillaic acid, and pioglitazone, all of which are known to interact with the same enzyme. The evidence suggests that Licoagroside D acts as a modulator of this pathway, potentially influencing the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn affects the methylation of histone H3 lysine 9. The shared target of these compounds implies a common mechanism of action, possibly involving the inhibition or activation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Licoagroside D in the regulation of histone methylation, suggesting a broader pharmacological impact on epigenetic processes.",
